"t":1736172986,"iso":"2025-01-06T14:16:26Z","rt":5,"replies":1,"quotes":0,"likes":22,"relation":"reply","niveau":2,"author":"Escape2SEA","author_id":"1239798356366385154","text":"2. Who is at Risk?\n\nHMPV can infect anyone, but some people are more at risk:\n\n• Young children (under 5 years old).\n\n• Older adults (over 65 years old).\n\n• People with weak immune systems, such as those with chronic illnesses or undergoing treatments like chemotherapy.\n\n•","in_corpus":true,"depth":2,"subtree_rt":27,"subtree_size":9,"dt_root_h":0.001,"parent_id":"1876271607703883778","conversation_id":"1876271603744432251"},{"id":"1876271615182553290","x":1.2e-05,"y":0.5,"t":1736172987,"iso":"2025-01-06T14:16:27Z","rt":6,"replies":1,"quotes":0,"likes":21,"relation":"reply","niveau":3,"author":"Escape2SEA","author_id":"1239798356366385154","text":"3. Symptoms of HMPV\n\nThe symptoms of HMPV are similar to the flu or a cold and include:\n\n• Fever.\n• Runny or stuffy nose.\n• Cough and sore throat.\n• Trouble breathing or wheezing.\n• Feeling tired or weak.\n\nIn severe cases, it can cause:\n\n• Bronchiolitis (inflammation in the","in_corpus":true,"depth":3,"subtree_rt":22,"subtree_size":8,"dt_root_h":0.001,"parent_id":"1876271610975424960","conversation_id":"1876271603744432251"},{"id":"1876271619686981814","x":1.6e-05,"y":0.5,"t":1736172988,"iso":"2025-01-06T14:16:28Z","rt":4,"replies":1,"quotes":0,"likes":12,"relation":"reply","niveau":4,"author":"Escape2SEA","author_id":"1239798356366385154","text":"4. Why is China Monitoring This Virus?\n\nChina has started watching this virus closely because:\n\n1. There are reports of more HMPV cases, especially in people who are at high risk.\n\n2. Other countries have also seen more HMPV cases recently.\n\n3. HMPV has symptoms similar to other","in_corpus":true,"depth":4,"subtree_rt":16,"subtree_size":7,"dt_root_h":0.001,"parent_id":"1876271615182553290","conversation_id":"1876271603744432251"},{"id":"1876271622996287559","x":2e-05,"y":0.5,"t":1736172989,"iso":"2025-01-06T14:16:29Z","rt":4,"replies":1,"quotes":0,"likes":11,"relation":"reply","niveau":5,"author":"Escape2SEA","author_id":"1239798356366385154","text":"5. How Does HMPV Spread?\n\nHMPV spreads through:\n\n• Respiratory droplets from coughing, sneezing, or talking.\n\n• Direct contact with an infected person.\n\n• Touching surfaces that have the virus and then touching your face.","in_corpus":true,"depth":5,"subtree_rt":12,"subtree_size":6,"dt_root_h":0.001,"parent_id":"1876271619686981814","conversation_id":"1876271603744432251"},{"id":"1876271626892853452","x":2e-05,"y":0.5,"t":1736172989,"iso":"2025-01-06T14:16:29Z","rt":3,"replies":1,"quotes":0,"likes":12,"relation":"reply","niveau":6,"author":"Escape2SEA","author_id":"1239798356366385154","text":"6. How to Prevent It?\n\nThere is no vaccine or specific treatment for HMPV, but you can reduce your risk by:\n\n1. Washing your hands often with soap and water.\n\n2. Wearing a mask in crowded places.\n\n3. Avoiding close contact with sick people.\n\n4. Cleaning surfaces that are","in_corpus":true,"depth":6,"subtree_rt":8,"subtree_size":5,"dt_root_h":0.001,"parent_id":"1876271622996287559","conversation_id":"1876271603744432251"},{"id":"1876271630281810323","x":2.4e-05,"y":0.5,"t":1736172990,"iso":"2025-01-06T14:16:30Z","rt":3,"replies":2,"quotes":0,"likes":17,"relation":"reply","niveau":7,"author":"Escape2SEA","author_id":"1239798356366385154","text":"7. Treatment\n\nThere’s no medicine that directly treats HMPV. Doctors focus on helping you feel better, such as:\n\n• Drinking lots of fluids.\n\n• Taking fever-reducing medicine like ibuprofen.\n\n• Using oxygen therapy if needed in severe cases.","in_corpus":true,"depth":7,"subtree_rt":5,"subtree_size":4,"dt_root_h":0.002,"parent_id":"1876271626892853452","conversation_id":"1876271603744432251"},{"id":"1876492118690337267","x":0.209577,"y":1.0,"t":1736225559,"iso":"2025-01-07T04:52:39.000Z","rt":0,"replies":0,"quotes":0,"likes":0,"relation":